9497	{"artifactId":"LLD-8ca7382b0952a539-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-8ca7382b0952a539-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:27:21.989Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new module covers the ISSUE's whole fix intent: it owns the lease, the generation/supersede rules and the running process; it lets the panel start, report, stop and ask whether a turn is running; and it gets its own unit tests.","evidence":"The ISSUE's fix intent (ISSUE.md:15) asks for: start a turn and wait for its lease, report events, stop, 'say whether one is running', own the lease, generation and supersede rules and the process, and unit tests. The LLD covers each one: start/stop/detach/invalidate, `live` (whether a turn is running), the state moved from chat-panel.ts:142-177, acquireSessionLease/runLeased/followLiveTurn/stopLive/stopActive/detachActive, and turn-lifecycle.test.ts. The panel keeps webview wiring, titles and permission/selection handling, as the ISSUE says it should. [files: docs/standalone/defect-vscode-plugin-src-chat-chat-E202610108ca7382b/ISSUE.md, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today, a superseded or disposed turn keeps reading but posts nothing. At its terminal event it clears its cursor and returns the iterator. Only the current generation posts the waiting status and the lock error.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:900-906: `if (disposed || myGen !== generation) { if (next.value.kind === 'done' || ... 'error') { clearCursor(...); void iterator.return?.(undefined); break; } continue; }`. Lines 757 and 765 gate the waiting post and the 'could not lock chat session' post on `!disposed && myGen === generation`. Line 762 returns silently on LockWaitAborted/LockWaitSuperseded, and lines 770-773 release the lease when the turn is no longer current after the grant. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today, a done/error event clears the cursor before the session is saved. Saving at a done uses the throwing deps.store.save, not trySave. A throw in the run posts an error with activeTurnId ?? 'none' and saves the session.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:931 runs `clearCursor(ev.turnId)` before the `deps.store.save(s)` calls at 934 and 941. Line 933 sets nativeSessionId on a done. The catch at 948-952 posts `{kind:'error', turnId: activeTurnId ?? 'none', ...}` and then calls trySave(s), only when current. This matches LLD §2.2 and the onTerminal note 'store.save, which may throw'. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The panel's call sites that the lifecycle must take over are complete: runTurn, followLiveTurn (postInitialState and open-chat), cancel-turn, new-chat/open-chat with their ++generation, the permission-decision relay, dispose, adopt, and channel onDidDispose.","evidence":"A grep of chat-panel.ts finds every use: stopActive at 1014 (cancel-turn); detachActive at 1026/1046 (each followed by ++generation at 1027/1047), 1181 (onDidDispose), 1203 (adopt) and 1214 (dispose); followLiveTurn at 339 (postInitialState) and 1052; activeProvider/activeTurnId at 1120-1122 (permission-decision, which the LLD maps to `live`). No other code outside the turn machinery reads generation, waitCtl, liveProc or runningTurns. extension.ts:52/588 imports DEFAULT_TURN_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS, and the LLD keeps that import working through a re-export. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"TurnLifecycleDeps.processStartTime has the type (pid: number) => number | null and takes what the panel resolves today.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:98 declares `readonly processStartTime?: ((pid: number) => number | undefined) | undefined;`. session-lock.ts:322 declares `export function defaultProcessStartTime(pid: number): number | undefined`. Line 851 turns undefined into null itself (`startTime(proc.pid) ?? null`). Under strict TS, passing the panel's resolved `startTime` into a dep typed `number | null` fails tsc. That breaks the LLD's own 'plugin tsc --noEmit clean' acceptance check. Type the dep as `number | undefined` and keep the `?? null` inside the module. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-lock.ts]","action":"Change TurnLifecycleDeps.processStartTime to `(pid: number) => number | undefined` (matching ChatPanelHostDeps and defaultProcessStartTime), and keep the `?? null` coercion when writing liveTurn.startedAt.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Invariant: Stop ends both the live turn and the followed turn. A chat switch, close or adopt only detaches a session-file turn and stops a pipe turn. The LLD's stop()/detach() reproduce stopActive/detachActive, and invalidate() reproduces the separate ++generation.","evidence":"stopActive (712-718) aborts following, stops resumedProc and calls stopLive. stopLive (678-709) aborts waitCtl, returns the iterator, calls providers.get(prov).cancel(tid) and stops liveProc, swallowing each failure. detachActive (725-739) detaches only when `detachLive !== undefined && liveProc?.cursor !== undefined` and otherwise calls stopLive. detachThis (888-893) removes the turn id from runningTurns and saves. The generation bump after detachActive is a separate statement (1027/1047), which matches the separate invalidate(). The LLD's stop, detach and invalidate contracts and its edge-case table match all of this. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Invariant: one CLI process per session. The lease is released when the process exits, not when its answer ends, through runLeased's attach in onSpawn. An adapter without onSpawn releases on return.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:829-834: `await runLeased(lease, async (attachLease) => { const onSpawn = (proc) => { attachLease(proc); ...`. session-lock.ts:142 exports `runLeased<T>(lease, body: (attach) => Promise<T>)`. The comment at 827-828 says it 'releases the lease on every path unless a process was attached'. The LLD moves this block unchanged into start() (§2.2 postconditions and the edge-case table). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-lock.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion has a test that fails without the fix. ac1 is proved by new turn-lifecycle.test.ts unit cases, one per lifecycle rule, using the existing fixtures (fakeLiveProc, waitFor, tick) and createMemorySessionLocks. ac2 is proved by the unchanged chat-panel and extension-wiring suites plus a clean tsc.","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.ts does not exist yet, so every ac1 unit case fails to import without the fix. The fixtures exist: __tests__/fixtures.ts:54 `export const tick`, :57 `export async function waitFor`, :82 `export function fakeLiveProc`. session-lock.ts:164 exports createMemorySessionLocks. The listed subjects cover every error path and edge case in §4 (supersede while waiting/reading, grant after stale, lock failure, throw in the run, cursor throttle and clear, stop idempotent, detach for session-file vs pipe, follow skip/takeover, invalidate, live). ac2 is a regression guard, and the extracted code must be in place for it to pass. One note: chat-panel.test.ts has 104 `test(`/`it(` lines, not the '111 cases' the LLD states. This does not affect the tests themselves. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/fixtures.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-lock.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts]","action":"Optionally correct the '111 cases' count for chat-panel.test.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":7,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-10T18:27:21.989Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"change-sites.2":{"findingId":"change-sites.2","status":"resolved","note":"Applied: TurnLifecycleDeps.processStartTime is now (pid: number) => number | undefined, matching ChatPanelHostDeps and defaultProcessStartTime; the module keeps the ?? null when writing liveTurn.startedAt.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-10T18:28:49.072Z"}}}}}}
